I routed the four model ids to yoagent 0.25.8's presets and committed it as 06fd4f83. Clippy and the full cargo test run (size gate included) pass.

What each id got before the change (measured with a throwaway probe that I then replaced with the real tests):
• `google/gemini-4-argon`, `gemini-3.8-flash`: a 1M window, max_tokens capped at 8192, and reasoning off. /cost had no entry for Argon. For Flash it matched the generic "gemini-3" estimate of $0.15/$0.60 instead of the real $1.50/$7.50.
• `xai/grok-4.7`, `mistral/mistral-large-4`: both were built from the generic OpenAI config, so they got a guessed 128K window, max_tokens 4096, and no price. /cost billed grok-4.7 at grok-4's $3/$15; the real price is $2/$6.

None of the four was already routed to a preset, so all four stayed in the task.

What changed:
• `vendor_preset(provider, id)`: a new helper in src/agent_builder.rs that matches the exact provider and id. It copies the preset's window, max_tokens, price and reasoning setting onto the provider's existing config, so base URL, compat and headers stay as they were. This follows the existing OpenAI preset pattern, and production code grew by 40 lines (4949, cap 4969).
• Places that now read the preset: /cost (including grok-4.7's higher rate for prompts of 200K tokens and up), the /model context-window figure, the known-model lists, and the "guessed limits" warning. The output-limit warning applies only to Google, which publishes 65,536 as the real maximum. xAI and Mistral publish no maximum, so their max_tokens is treated as a default and no warning is given.
• Docs: docs/src/configuration/models.md and the helper's doc comment say that Argon, 3.8 Flash and Mistral Large 4 are priced at the regular rate, so /cost can show up to twice the actual bill while the vendors' launch or introductory pricing runs.

Tests: 9 new tests in src/provider_presets_tests.rs, declared in main.rs like the other preset test files. Every expected value is read from yoagent's own constructor rather than typed in. Near misses like gemini-3.8-flash-lite, grok-4.7-mini and mistral-large-latest keep their old values, and the same ids on another provider don't get the preset. As a check, I broke the grok-4.7 match on purpose: 5 of the 9 tests failed, and I restored it in the same command.

The commit is local; this session's push is what puts it on main. I've already posted a comment on #1037 naming the four ids and the sha, since a "Part of" commit doesn't update the issue on its own.

Still open on #1021/#1037: default models for google, xai and mistral; presets for zai glm-5.3 and qwen3.8; and the stale gemini-3.0 ids in commands.rs and commands_info.rs.
